#: src/public/privacy.html:11
#: src/public/privacy.html:20
msgid "Privacy Policy"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:12
msgid "What Starter Pack collects, why, who it shares it with, and how to delete it."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:21
#: src/public/terms.html:21
msgid "Effective [Effective date]"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:24
msgid "This policy explains what [Company name] (\"we\", \"us\") collects when you use Starter Pack on the web, the desktop or a phone, why, who we share it with, and the choices you have. We do not sell your personal data, and we do not use it for advertising."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:29
msgid "1. What we collect"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:31
msgid "<strong>Your account</strong>: your name, your email address, and a password if you set one (stored only as a secure hash). We email you codes to sign in and to confirm changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:33
msgid "<strong>Your content</strong>: posts, files and pictures you add, the communities you make or join, and your profile picture."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:35
msgid "<strong>Purchases</strong>: which plan or product you bought, its price and currency, its status and dates, and the store's ids for it. We never see or store your card details: Stripe or Apple holds them."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:38
msgid "<strong>Technical data</strong>: your IP address and requests, which our servers use to keep the service secure and to limit abuse, and keep in short-lived server logs."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:40
msgid "<strong>On your devices</strong>: the apps keep a copy of your content so they work offline, and data you keep in an app before signing up stays on that device and is never sent to us."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:44
msgid "2. Why we use it"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:46
msgid "To run the service: your account, signing in, syncing your content between your devices and with the people you share it with (performing our contract with you)."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:48
msgid "To take payments and provide what you bought (contract)."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:49
msgid "To keep the service secure, prevent abuse and fix problems (our legitimate interests)."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:50
msgid "To email you about your account, such as sign-in codes, purchases and changes to these policies (contract and legitimate interests). We do not send marketing email without your consent."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:52
msgid "To meet legal obligations, such as tax and accounting records."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:55
msgid "3. Who we share it with"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:56
msgid "We share personal data only with the providers who run parts of the service for us:"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:58
msgid "<strong>Stripe</strong>, which takes payments on the web and the desktop as the merchant of record (Stripe Managed Payments) and receives your email and billing details for that."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:60
msgid "<strong>Apple</strong>, which takes payments in the iPhone and iPad app through the App Store. Apple tells us about the purchase, with an id that links it to your account, not your Apple ID's details."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:62
msgid "<strong>[Hosting provider]</strong>, which hosts our servers, database and file storage."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:63
msgid "<strong>[Email provider]</strong>, which sends our emails."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:66
msgid "Your content is also visible to the members of the communities you post in. We disclose data when the law requires it, and to a buyer of our business, who would be bound by this policy."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:70
msgid "4. Cookies and browser storage"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:72
msgid "On the web we use one cookie, to keep you signed in. We use no analytics, advertising or tracking cookies. Your browser also keeps a few settings of yours, such as your theme and whether you are signed in, in its local storage, which never leaves your device."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:77
msgid "5. How long we keep it"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:79
msgid "Your account and content: while your account exists. Content you delete is removed from our database 90 days later, which gives your devices time to see the delete."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:81
msgid "When you delete your account, your content is deleted at once in every community and on every device as it syncs, your files and pictures are deleted from storage at once, and the rest is removed from our database within 90 days."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:84
msgid "A trial on the web without an account: deleted after two days."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:85
msgid "Payment records that the law requires us to keep, such as invoices, are kept by Stripe or Apple for as long as it requires."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:87
msgid "Backups are overwritten within [Backup retention, e.g. 30 days]."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:90
msgid "6. Your choices and rights"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:92
msgid "You can see and change your name, email, picture and content in the service, and delete your account at any time in the app's account settings. Depending on where you live, you may also have the right to ask for a copy of your data, to correct or erase it, to object to or restrict how we use it, to move it to another service, and to complain to your data protection authority. To use any of these rights, email [Contact email]; we answer within 30 days."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:99
msgid "7. Security"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:101
msgid "Data travels encrypted between your devices and our servers. Passwords are stored only as hashes, sign-in codes expire within minutes, and access to our systems is limited to the people who run them. No system is perfectly secure; we will tell you and the authorities of a breach that affects you, as the law requires."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:106
msgid "8. Where it is processed"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:108
msgid "We and our providers may process data in [Countries, e.g. the United States] and other countries. Where the law requires, transfers are covered by safeguards such as the European Commission's standard contractual clauses."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:113
msgid "9. Children"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:115
msgid "The service is not meant for children under [16]. We do not knowingly collect their data; if you believe a child has given us data, email [Contact email] and we will delete it."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:119
msgid "10. Changes to this policy"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:121
msgid "We will post changes here with their effective date and, for changes that matter, tell you by email or in the service before they apply."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:125
msgid "11. Contact"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/privacy.html:127
msgid "[Company name], [Postal address]. Email: [Contact email]. [Data protection officer or EU/UK representative, if you need one.] See also our <a href=\"/terms\" class=\"link\">Terms of Service</a>."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:11
#: src/public/terms.html:20
msgid "Terms of Service"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:12
msgid "The terms for using Starter Pack on the web, the desktop and phones."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:24
msgid "These terms are an agreement between you and [Company name] (\"we\", \"us\") for using Starter Pack: the website, the web application, and the desktop and phone apps (together, \"the service\"). By creating an account or using the service you accept these terms and our <a href=\"/privacy\" class=\"link\">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not accept them, do not use the service."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:30
msgid "1. Your account"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:32
msgid "You sign up with your name and an email address, which we confirm by sending a code. You may also set a password. You must be at least [16] years old, or the age of digital consent where you live, to have an account. Keep your sign-in codes, password and signed-in devices safe; you are responsible for what is done with your account."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:38
msgid "You may try the service without an account. A trial on the web is deleted after two days unless you sign up. Data you keep in an app on a device before signing up stays on that device and is not sent to us."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:42
msgid "2. Your content"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:44
msgid "You keep ownership of what you put in the service: posts, files, pictures and anything else (\"your content\"). You give us a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to store, copy, sync and show your content only as needed to run the service for you and for the people you share it with, such as the other members of a community. This license ends when your content is deleted from the service."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:50
msgid "You are responsible for your content and must have the right to share it. Content you post in a community is visible to that community's members, and copies of it are kept on their devices so the apps work offline."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:55
msgid "3. Acceptable use"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:56
msgid "You agree not to:"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:58
msgid "break the law, or help anyone else to;"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:59
msgid "post content that infringes others' rights, or that is abusive, harassing, hateful or sexual content involving minors;"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:61
msgid "send spam, malware, or anything meant to harm the service or other people;"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:62
msgid "try to get into accounts or systems that are not yours, or test or overload the service without our written permission;"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:64
msgid "resell the service or use it to build a competing one by copying it."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:67
msgid "We may remove content or suspend or end an account that breaks these terms, and we will tell you when we can."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:71
msgid "4. Plans and purchases"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:73
msgid "Some features need a paid plan or a one-time purchase. Prices and what each includes are shown before you buy. A purchase belongs to your account and works on the web, the desktop and phones."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:78
msgid "<strong>On the web and the desktop</strong> payments are taken by Stripe, which acts as the merchant of record (Stripe Managed Payments): it charges you, collects any sales tax or VAT, and its terms also apply to the payment."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:83
msgid "<strong>In the iPhone and iPad app</strong> payments are taken by Apple through the App Store, under Apple's terms, and Apple's Licensed Application End User License Agreement applies to the app."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:88
msgid "A plan is a subscription that renews automatically at the end of each period, monthly or yearly, at the price then shown, until you cancel it. You can cancel at any time: a plan bought on the web or desktop in your account's settings, a plan bought in the App Store in your Apple ID's subscription settings. After cancelling, the plan lasts until the end of the period already paid. A renewal that cannot be paid ends the plan's features until it is paid."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:95
msgid "Except where the law requires otherwise, payments are not refunded. You may ask us for a refund of a Stripe payment at [Contact email]; refunds of App Store payments are made by Apple. We may change a plan's price with notice before your next renewal; you can cancel before it applies."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:100
msgid "5. Deleting your account"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:102
msgid "You can delete your account at any time in the app's account settings. This deletes your content in every community and on every device, cancels a plan bought through Stripe at once without a refund, and cannot be undone. A plan bought in the App Store must be cancelled in the App Store, or Apple keeps billing it. Deleted data is removed from our systems within 90 days, as the <a href=\"/privacy\" class=\"link\">Privacy Policy</a> describes."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:109
msgid "6. The service"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:111
msgid "We work to keep the service running and your data safe, and we may change, add or remove features. The apps sync with our servers when they are online; changes made offline are sent later and may conflict with others' changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:116
msgid "THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\" AND \"AS AVAILABLE\", WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT, TO THE EXTENT THE LAW ALLOWS. Keep your own copies of anything you cannot afford to lose."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:121
msgid "7. Limit of liability"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:123
msgid "TO THE EXTENT THE LAW ALLOWS, [COMPANY NAME] IS NOT LIABLE FOR INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR FOR LOST PROFITS, DATA OR GOODWILL, AND OUR TOTAL LIABILITY FOR ANY CLAIM ABOUT THE SERVICE IS LIMITED TO THE GREATER OF WHAT YOU PAID US IN THE TWELVE MONTHS BEFORE THE CLAIM AND [100 USD]. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:129
msgid "You will compensate [Company name] for claims by others arising from your content or your breach of these terms, to the extent the law allows."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:133
msgid "8. Changes to these terms"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:135
msgid "We may update these terms. We will post the new terms here with their effective date and, for changes that matter, tell you by email or in the service before they apply. Using the service after that means you accept them."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:140
msgid "9. Law and disputes"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:142
msgid "These terms are governed by the laws of [Governing law, e.g. the State of Delaware, USA], without regard to its conflict-of-law rules, and disputes are settled in the courts of [Venue]. If you are a consumer, you keep the protections of the law where you live."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:147
msgid "If part of these terms cannot be enforced, the rest still applies. These terms and the Privacy Policy are the whole agreement between you and us about the service."
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:151
msgid "10. Contact"
msgstr ""

#: src/public/terms.html:152
msgid "[Company name], [Postal address]. Email: [Contact email]."
msgstr ""
